# Revisions to skip when running `git blame`.
#
# Only bulk revisions with no behavioural change belong here: mechanical
# Clippy fixes (`#[must_use]`, `const fn`, trailing-semicolon and `format!`
# consistency) and the pure `git mv` commits of the package-by-feature
# migration, which move files without touching a single byte of content.
# See SPEC-package-by-feature.md sections 9.5 and 13.1.
#
# Never add a revision that changes behaviour: doing so hides the real author
# of that behaviour from `git blame` permanently.
#
# GitHub honours this file automatically. Locally, enable it once with:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Entries are full 40-character SHAs, one per line, newest last.
